# {{senseid|en|personification}} {{lb|en|often|capitalized}} The [[personification]] of death as a (usually male) [[hooded]] figure with a [[scythe]]; the [[Grim Reaper]].
#: {{ux|en|When '''death''' walked in, a chill spread through the room.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Revelation|6|8|passage=And I looked, and behold, a pale horse, & his name that sat on him was '''Death'''"}}
#* {{RQ:Sterne Tristram Shandy|volume=V|chapter=IX|page=51|passage=[T]o thoſe, ''Jonathan'', who know what '''death''' is, and what havock and deſtruction he can make, before a man can well wheel about—'tis like a whole age.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1974|author=Anthony Banks; Michael Rutherford; w:Peter Gabriel; w:Phil Collins; Steve Hackett|album=w:The Lamb Lies Down on Broadway|title=Anyway|artist=Genesis|passage=O boy! running man is out of '''death''' ... Anyway, they say she comes on a pale horse}}
# {{senseid|en|end}} {{lb|en|preceded by [[the]]}} The [[collapse]] or [[end]] of something.
#: {{ux|en|England scored a goal at the '''death''' to even the score at one all.}}
#: {{ux|en|''Buyer (negotiating):'' You were at two-fifty on that one. Go on, then, what's the '''death''' on that? ''Seller:'' Two hundred pounds is the absolute '''death'''. ''Buyer:'' Sold. Thank you.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author=Robert R. Faulkner|title=Music on Demand|page=90
|passage=He may even find himself being blamed if the project dies a quick and horrible '''death''' at the box office or is unceremoniously axed by the network.}}
